# Line endings. Every text file is LF in the repository and in every working copy, whatever
# `core.autocrlf` says. A Windows checkout with autocrlf on would otherwise turn the render goldens
# (byte-exact, the Java engine's acceptance test) and every file Prettier checks red. Prettier's own
# `endOfLine` default is "lf", so the two agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact fixtures: tests read these from disk and compare them with what the code produces, so
# git never converts them, in either direction. None holds a CR today; `-text` is what lets one that
# should (a clipboard capture from Word on Windows has CRLFs) be committed as it is. Keep this list
# in step with the "Byte-exact fixtures" group in .prettierignore.
/src/server/render/golden/cases/** -text
/src/editor/paste/__fixtures__/** -text
/e2e/fixtures/import/** -text
/src/domain/messages/GraphemeBreakTest.txt -text

# Binary files: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
